"text": "The gates run the agent-run contract's cases (the six new ones named, each by unittest's verbose line), the `ci-scripts` leg they ride in CI, and the smoke this chunk builds, through the contract itself: `boot`, then `run session`, then `status`, each asserting the event the script prints (its form from `agent-run.sh:106-115` and `:136-138`, keys in that order, python's `json.dumps` spacing). The `run session` entry IS the chunk's `role = 'smoke'` entry: the touched script is the harness every smoke runs through. It has no `leg`: the contract mints no id, and a reader may re-run it (scope, premise corrected at P3). No live leg — nothing outside the tree is driven. The new cases' red-before-green is step 1's recorded reading against HEAD's script (test-plan · decision/mutation-controlled-tests), not a `gate.py control`: the tool reads libtest, nextest and pytest result lines, and unittest's `… ok` / `FAIL` form is none of them (gate-contract.md §Control, *Limits*; no pytest on the host, `python3 -m pytest --version`: `No module named pytest`). The `cli_flow` target carries its own red control (`cli_flow.rs:76-88`, the flow handed `true` reads `step 1`, status 1). The diff is a shell script whose new arm reaches a `#![cfg(unix)]` target: off unix the `session` selection reads an empty run. No CI leg runs `agent-run.sh` itself on any OS (its contract tests run on linux under a `cargo` shim), so the plan carries the operator's hygiene, push and CI entries, and the CI entry's note says what witnesses what."
}
],
